            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0392" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–2848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-28T10:00:00+09:00">July 28, 1948—10
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 28—3:47 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. My telegram 316 yesterday. Students continued parade through city until 1630
                    hours, without serious incident and with no anti-foreign expression. Marchers
                    orderly but evidenced genuine feeling. Police vicinity demonstrators did not
                    bear arms.</p>
                <p>All non-military rail traffic Mukden area halted yesterday morning by strike,
                    workers demanded food allowance equal that railway workers in intramural China
                    and immediate payment wages in arrears, No violence. Demands accepted early
                    today and traffic resumed.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 399; repeated Department 318.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
